INK['theft'] = (f'- THE THEFT AND THE GIFTS: "any of the sins of man" at {KOL_CHATOT[0]} alone; the fifth-clause at {", ".join(FIFTH)}; "the ram of atonements" and "the guilt restored" at 5:8 alone; "a man\'s holy things are his" at {KODASHAV[0]} alone; THE TRESPASS-NOUN BY ITS POINTS: מַעַל ("trespass", a patach — the short a-vowel — under both letters) at {len(MAAL_NOUN)} Tanakh seats against מֵעַל ("from upon", a tsere — the long e-vowel) at {MAAL_FROM} — the same consonants; 5:12\'s verb {MAAL_VERB512} ("she trespassed", the pausal form). Onkelos renders every trespass by LYING (5:6, 5:12, 5:27) — the Sifrei\'s lemma rule (piskaot 2, 7) is the translation\'s word.')
