INK['seven_seats'] = f'- CHAPTER SEVEN\'S CENSUS IDIOMS: 7:2 "they who stood over the counted" — the princes of 1:4-16 and the counters of 4:34, 4:46; 7:3\'s "six... twelve... two... one"; the wagon-word צב rendered "covered" (Rebbi\'s arm); the pan-word and the dish-word of 7:13-14 are 4:7\'s (the table\'s vessels); the shekel written as the sela at every weight (7:13, 7:14, 7:85, 7:86 — the conversion layer one to one, Bekhorot 50a).'
def register_line(c, lo, hi): return f'- THE REGISTER: {register(c, lo, hi)} — the narrative verbs of the span (the narrative-past "and he did" form, the register test).'

